.*
.* WRKSPLF: the spooled files of a user, of a job or of everyone. F11
.* steps through three views: where each file is, its form and number,
.* and its job and creation time.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NBRCL BASETYPE='CHAR 6'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=STSCL BASETYPE='CHAR 3'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PAGECL BASETYPE='ZONED 5 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=CURPCL BASETYPE='ZONED 5 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=COPYCL BASETYPE='ZONED 3 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PTYCL BASETYPE='CHAR 1'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=DATECL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VIEWCL BASETYPE='CHAR 1'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=FILE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=DEVQ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=USRDTA CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=STS CLASS=STSCL.
:VAR NAME=PAGES CLASS=PAGECL.
:VAR NAME=CURPAGE CLASS=CURPCL.
:VAR NAME=COPIES CLASS=COPYCL.
:VAR NAME=JOB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=NUMBER CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=SPLNBR CLASS=NBRCL.
:VAR NAME=FORMTYPE CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=PTY CLASS=PTYCL.
:VAR NAME=CRTDATE CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=CRTTIME CLASS=DATECL.
:VAR NAME=VIEW CLASS=VIEWCL VALUE='1'.
:LISTDEF NAME=FILES VARS='OPT FILE USER DEVQ USRDTA STS PAGES CURPAGE COPIES JOB NUMBER SPLNBR FORMTYPE PTY CRTDATE CRTTIME'.
:COND NAME=VIEW1 EXPR='&VIEW. EQ "1"'.
:COND NAME=VIEW2 EXPR='&VIEW. EQ "2"'.
:COND NAME=VIEW3 EXPR='&VIEW. EQ "3"'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/SPLKEYS' NAME=SPLKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F10 ACTION='RETURN 10'.F10=View 4
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=VIEW1.F11=View 2
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=VIEW2.F11=View 3
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11' COND=VIEW3.F11=View 1
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='CMD WRKWTR'.F22=Printers
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKSPLF KEYL=SPLKEYS HELP=WRKSPLF ENTER='RETURN 1'.Work with All Spooled Files
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=FILES MAXHEAD=3 VIEWS=3.(No spooled files to show)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ENTER='CMD ?SNDNETSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.1=Send
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGSPLFA FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=3 ENTER='CMD HLDSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.3=Hold
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ENTER='CMD DLTSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ENTER='CMD DSPSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.5=Display
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ENTER='CMD RLSSPLF FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.6=Release
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=7 ENTER='RETURN 7'.7=Messages
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ENTER='CMD WRKSPLFA FILE(&FILE.) JOB(&NUMBER./&USER./&JOB.) SPLNBR(&SPLNBR.)'.8=Attributes
:LISTACT HELP='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS' OPTION=9 ENTER='RETURN 9'.9=Work with printing status
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKSPLF/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/FILE' VAR=FILE USAGE=OUTPUT.File
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/USER' VAR=USER USAGE=OUTPUT.User
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/DEVQ' VAR=DEVQ USAGE=OUTPUT.Device or Queue
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/USRDTA' VAR=USRDTA USAGE=OUTPUT.User Data
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/STS' VAR=STS USAGE=OUTPUT.Sts
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/PAGES' VAR=PAGES USAGE=OUTPUT.Total Pages
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/CURPAGE' VAR=CURPAGE USAGE=OUTPUT.Cur Page
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/COPIES' VAR=COPIES USAGE=OUTPUT.Copy
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/FORMTYPE' VAR=FORMTYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Form Type
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/PTY' VAR=PTY USAGE=OUTPUT.Pty
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/SPLNBR' VAR=SPLNBR USAGE=OUTPUT.File Nbr
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/JOB' VAR=JOB USAGE=OUTPUT.Job
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/NUMBER' VAR=NUMBER USAGE=OUTPUT.Number
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/CRTDATE' VAR=CRTDATE USAGE=OUTPUT.Date
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/CRTTIME' VAR=CRTTIME USAGE=OUTPUT.Time
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT FILE USER DEVQ USRDTA STS PAGES CURPAGE COPIES'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT FILE USER DEVQ FORMTYPE PTY SPLNBR'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT FILE SPLNBR JOB USER NUMBER CRTDATE CRTTIME'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 2, 3 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKSPLF.Work with All Spooled Files - Help
:P.The spooled files asked for, oldest first, with where each waits or
prints. Type an option next to a file, or a command on the command
line. F11 shows each file's form type, priority and number, then the
job that made it and when: files of the same name are told apart by
those.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SPLKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F10=View 4
:PD.View 4.
:PT.F11=View 2
:PD.View 2.
:PT.F11=View 3
:PD.View 3.
:PT.F11=View 1
:PD.View 1.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F22=Printers
:PD.Runs WRKWTR.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSPLF/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FILE'.File
:P.The file, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DEVQ'.Device or Queue
:P.The device or Queue of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USRDTA'.User Data
:P.User data, up to 10 characters, kept with the object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STS'.Sts
:P.The sts of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PAGES'.Total Pages
:P.The total Pages of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CURPAGE'.Cur Page
:P.The cur Page of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/COPIES'.Copy
:P.The copy of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FORMTYPE'.Form Type
:P.The type of form the output is printed on. The writer stops for the
form to be loaded when it changes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PTY'.Pty
:P.The pty of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SPLNBR'.File Nbr
:P.The file Nbr of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/JOB'.Job
:P.The job, by name, user and number. A job name alone is enough when
only one job has it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/NUMBER'.Number
:P.The number of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CRTDATE'.Date
:P.The date of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CRTTIME'.Time
:P.The time of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSPLF/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Send
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to send it. The Send Network
Spooled File (SNDNETSPLF) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Spooled File Attr (CHGSPLFA) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Hold
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to hold it. The Hold Spooled
File (HLDSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Spooled File (DLTSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Spooled File (DSPSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.6=Release
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to release it. The Release
Spooled File (RLSSPLF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.7=Messages
:PD.Type 7 next to an entry and press Enter to messages it.
:PT.8=Attributes
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to attributes it. The Work
with Spooled File Attributes (WRKSPLFA) command runs for the entry.
:PT.9=Work with printing status
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to work with printing status
it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
